Alice, all,

Good news -- rollback procedure is now fully documented, including Scenario 4.

Scenario 4: Auth service dependency failure
  - v2 auth middleware falls back to cached JWT validation (15-min TTL)
  - If cache is cold, route affected endpoints to v1 (session-based auth)
  - Alert on-call auth team via PagerDuty
  - Estimated impact: degraded experience for ~2% of requests during failover

I also added a "decision tree" flowchart to the runbook so whoever is on-call
can quickly determine which scenario we're in and follow the right steps.

Here's the final runbook summary:

  Step | Action                              | Owner  | ETA
  -----|-------------------------------------|--------|--------
  1    | Start DB migration (indexes)        | Alice  | T-2h
  2    | Verify index creation completed     | Alice  | T-1h15m
  3    | Enable v2 shadow traffic (10%)      | Dave   | T-30m
  4    | Monitor error rates for 15 min      | Bob    | T-15m
  5    | Shift to 50% traffic                | Dave   | T+0
  6    | Monitor for 30 min                  | Bob    | T+30m
  7    | Shift to 100% traffic               | Dave   | T+1h
  8    | Monitor for 1 hour                  | Carol  | T+2h
  9    | Disable v1 write endpoints          | Alice  | T+3h
  10   | Send completion notice to team      | Alice  | T+3h

Everything on my end is ready. Green light from me for Friday.

- Dave

